# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Patterns map (one shape, one base)

> **Least code.** Pattern family = the rule of TWO applied to SHAPE: the same shape twice → ONE generic base, and each member supplies only its model/type and endpoint (`ProvidersService extends BaseApiService<Provider>`).
> TS utility types (`Partial`, `Pick`, `Omit`, `Record`, `ReturnType`, …) replace hand-written variants.
> The same-behaviour test decides per member: members that would not change together do not share a base; forcing one is over-abstraction.

How the file is kept: each project block opens with a `map-refresh: scan` marker comment that names
the scan date and the project. Its rows regenerate on every refresh; the ✍ columns are human text
and the refresh preserves them. Kind `family` = classes extending one local base; `shape` = files
whose name ends in the same role (`*.service.ts`); `types` = TS utility-type uses. Status is
`applied` (at least half the members extend the base), `partial k/n` (only k of n do) or a candidate
shape, which is a signal only. Evidence starts with the count (members, or uses for `types:utility`),
then the base or the per-type counts, then up to five paths. Edit only the ✍ cells, the Curated table
and the Retired table.

